  "_note": "order_docket layout draft (ORDER-rooted, OrderResult + items[]), A4 portrait 210x297 -- the first docket with a repeating positions table, so unlike the other four files in this folder this is NOT yet parseable by docket_spec.py: 'table', the per-block 'pages' scope and the @-prefixed renderer-provided fields (@page_number/@page_count/@page_label/@row_count/@item_image) are the PLANNED spec extension. Layout agreed 2026-08-14..16 and verified live against dev order BN-26-00003 (#57, 5 positions, S3 part images + logo) via the scratchpad prototype script (order_docket_prototype.py), which generates these exact blocks in code; multi-page pagination verified with rows x4 -> 2 pages. Geometry: frame 8..202 x 8..289; header grid columns x 14/64/114 (widths 46/46/44), label 2.6mm over bold 5mm value; QR 30mm at 164,29 -> @resolve_url on the order's own public_id (frontend routeForResolved already lands on /procurement/orders/{id}); header closes with a rule at y=66 clear of the last value row (~63.5). Table band starts AT that rule on page 1 (first_page_top_mm 66) and at y=30 on continuation pages under a compact strap (title + order number); capacity (280-top-8)/22 -> 9 rows page 1, 11 per continuation. Stacked cells: first field bold 3.5mm at row_top+4 (article stack: +3.5), following fields regular 3.0mm at +9 and +13.5, empty lines stay blank without reflow; image box keeps ~3mm air each side (block 20mm inside the 26mm column). Column-header labels vertically centred in the 8mm band (top offset 2.2), underline at band_top+7.5, row separators 0.15mm. Footer: bare date left, '1 / 3'-style @page_label right, nothing centre. Pending backend work this file assumes: item.* row namespace, product_number/total_items/orderer_full_name/delivered_by_full_name denormalizations, and the paginator that expands 'table' into per-page blocks -- see field_map comments below. Not print-tested.",
